# Sample data kept for reference but read by no server code — confirmed by
# searching the whole repository, not just src/. These six stay in the
# repository as reference material; they just stop being installed on the
# server, where nothing would ever read them.
#
# BEFORE ADDING A WILDCARD HERE, read this. The files under data/ that the
# running server opens are acc.json, accounts.json, first.json, lboard.json,
# build-number, the database it creates itself — and data/factions.tar.gz,
# which is the game download served by GET /download. That last one is easy to
# miss: it is not in git (it is built separately and placed on the server), so
# it is invisible when you list this folder on your own machine. A broad rule
# like `data/*.gz` would make the client download answer 404 in production, and
# no test would catch it — the download tests only cover the absent case.
# List files here one by one.
data/acc-backup.json
data/acc-new-units.json
data/battle.json
data/battlereadyData.json
data/battleDataStructure.txt
data/client-README.txt
